{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 1 from conj:four-term-pair-nucleon","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-four-term-pair-nucleon"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data\"></a><p>Normal form in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code> of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma\\gamma</code> product, with the photon <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma(\\varphi) = \\mathbf{1} + \\varphi_0\\sigma_0 + \\varphi_1\\sigma_1 + \\varphi_{01}\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1}</code> (<a href=\"#def:photon\" data-at=\"brings-surface/archimedean-condition-genus-completeness\">photon</a>), evaluated at the proton <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>. The basis words are <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+ = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_- = \\sigma_1\\sigma_0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Basis</th>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma(\\varphi)^2</code>, illustrative weights</th>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma_+\\gamma_-</code>, eigenvalue pair</th>\n<th align=\"left\">Role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+1.004</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.998</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Photon identity (vacuum)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.090</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.010</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Horizontal polarization</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.099</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.009</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Vertical polarization</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.043</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.046</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+ = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_-</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.003</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.044</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Cross-color <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_- = \\sigma_1\\sigma_0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+0.002</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Electron-word channel (4-term only)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The first column uses <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi = (0.0487, 0.0487, 0.02)</code> for both photons. These weights are not derived. The value <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.0487</code> is a fit to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2m_e</code> (Breit--Wheeler), and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.02</code> has no source; both were reconstructed by matching the earlier rounded entries of this table. The column is a worked illustration of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma\\gamma</code> normal form, not a prediction. The second column uses the eigenvalue pair <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma_\\pm</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi_0 = \\varphi_1 = 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi_{01} = qh</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-1}h</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code>, for which <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma_+\\gamma_- = (\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^3</code>. It is a product of two different photons and has no <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code> term.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data.md","heading":"Table","page":"b/tbl-four-term-pair-nucleon-table1-data","qa":{"counts":{"pass":40,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":57}}}
